            <ArticleTitle>[Changes in proinflammatory cytokine and destructive metalloproteinase levels during formation of unstable atherosclerotic plaque].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied men with coronary atherosclerosis without acute coronary syndrome and determined typical valuable parameters of inflammatory (tumor necrotic factor, antagonist of receptor to interleukin [IL] 1, IL 6, IL 8, monocytes chemotactic protein 1, endothelial monocytes activating protein II), and destructive (matrix metalloproteinase [MMP] 3, MMP 7, MMP 9, tissue inhibitor of metalloproteinase) processes at consecutive stages of formation of coronary atherosclerotic plaque: &quot;normal intimal tissue --&gt; lipid stain --&gt; early stable plaque --&gt; unstable vulnerable plaque &lt;--&gt; stable plaque with fibrosis&quot;, and in 3 types of unstable plaques (lipid type, inflammatory erosive type, necrotic type).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
